        <mxCell id="notes-dfs" parent="1" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=#147EBA;fillColor=#E6F2FF;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;fontSize=9;fontColor=#333333;rounded=1;arcSize=5;spacingLeft=5;spacingTop=3;" value="&lt;b&gt;Architecture Notes:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. &lt;b&gt;ALB + 7 ASGs (one per app)&lt;/b&gt;. HTTPS:443 (TLS termination,&lt;br&gt;   SNI with ACM certs) + HTTP:80, host-based routing.&lt;br&gt;   Backend IIS on HTTP:80. Scaling: CPU Target Tracking 70%.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;2. &lt;b&gt;3 standalone EC2&lt;/b&gt; (module ec2_windows): fixed hostname/IP,&lt;br&gt;   AD domain-joined, no FSx mount, not behind ALB.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;3. &lt;b&gt;ACM&lt;/b&gt;: 11 certs (1 per public host_header), external DNS&lt;br&gt;   validation. Expiration alarms -&gt; SNS acm-cert-expiration.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;4. &lt;b&gt;ASG Lifecycle Hook (leave-domain)&lt;/b&gt;: on scale-in, EventBridge&lt;br&gt;   triggers Lambda that runs Leave-Domain via SSM.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;5. &lt;b&gt;1x FSx (Single-AZ 1)&lt;/b&gt; for DFS-R, with its own CMK.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;6. &lt;b&gt;2x RDS SQL Server SE&lt;/b&gt;: produccion (Multi-AZ, r6i.4xl, 1.7TB, TDE)&lt;br&gt;   + procesos (Single-AZ, r6i.2xl, 2.9TB).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;7. &lt;b&gt;DMS&lt;/b&gt;: 8 CDC tasks one-way On-Premises to RDS produccion&lt;br&gt;   (8 DBs) via VPN/Direct Connect. Reverse direction commented.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;8. On-Premise DFS-R to dedicated file servers for DR." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="340" width="410" x="1480" y="800" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
